SECTION 2 - LETTER / COMPOSITION (30 marks)

You have a French pen-friend in Guadeloupe called Lucie. Write a letter of about 130 to 150 words in French in which you:

  - say how you are and when you received her letter;
  - describe what you have been doing at school this year (present tense);
  - describe something you did recently that you enjoyed (past tense);
  - explain what you are going to do in the summer holidays (future tense);
  - ask her at least one question about her own life.

Begin the letter with a greeting and end it with a suitable closing. Use the three tenses asked for - present, past and future. This section carries 30 marks.
